.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
.Dd November 7, 2026
.Dt YKUSHCTRL 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ykushctrl
.Nd control a Yepkit YKUSH3 switchable USB hub over USB HID
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl s Ar SERIAL
.Op Fl -no-wait
.Ar COMMAND
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
switches the three downstream USB 3.0 ports and the external 5 V output of a
Yepkit YKUSH3 board (VID 0x04D8, PID 0xF11B), configures their power-on state,
drives the three GPIO pins, and speaks to the board's I2C bridge.
A leading
.Cm ykush3
argument is accepted and ignored for compatibility with Yepkit's
.Ic ykushcmd .
.Pp
Two invocations addressing the same board take turns: on Linux through an
advisory
.Xr flock 2
on the board's
.Pa /dev/hidrawN
node, on FreeBSD through the single-open
.Xr hidraw 4
node itself, and on macOS through an exclusive IOKit open.
A second invocation waits up to five seconds for the board, or fails at once
with
.Fl -no-wait .
.Ss Port commands
.Ar PORT
is
.Cm 1 , 2
or
.Cm 3
for the downstream USB ports,
.Cm 4
or
.Cm e
for the external 5 V output, or
.Cm a
for all three downstream ports at once.
.Bl -tag -width "--i2c-set-address ADDR"
.It Fl u Ar PORT
Power
.Ar PORT
up.
.It Fl d Ar PORT
Power
.Ar PORT
down.
.It Fl g Ar PORT
Print whether
.Ar PORT
is on
.Pq Ql on
or off
.Pq Ql off ,
one line per port.
.It Fl on
Shorthand for
.Fl u Cm 4 .
.It Fl off
Shorthand for
.Fl d Cm 4 .
.It Fl c Ar PORT Ar STATE
Configure what single port
.Ar PORT
.Pq Cm 1 | 2 | 3 | 4 | e
does after a reset or power cut:
.Cm 0
stay off,
.Cm 1
come up,
.Cm 2
restore the state it had before losing power.
.El
.Ss GPIO commands
.Ar PIN
is
.Cm 1 , 2
or
.Cm 3 ;
.Ar LEVEL
is
.Cm 0
or
.Cm 1 .
.Bl -tag -width "--i2c-set-address ADDR"
.It Fl r Ar PIN
Read the logic level of
.Ar PIN
and print
.Ql 0
or
.Ql 1 .
.It Fl w Ar PIN Ar LEVEL
Drive
.Ar PIN
low
.Pq Cm 0
or high
.Pq Cm 1 .
.It Fl -gpio Cm enable | disable
Hand the GPIO pins over to the board to switch the like-numbered downstream
ports, or take them back for
.Fl r
and
.Fl w .
Takes effect after the next reset or power cut.
.El
.Ss I2C commands
Addresses and bytes are hexadecimal, with or without a
.Ql 0x
prefix.
7-bit I2C addresses are aligned to the top of the byte (write
.Ql 0xA2
for address
.Ql 0x51 ) .
.Bl -tag -width "--i2c-set-address ADDR"
.It Fl -i2c-slave Cm enable | disable
Enable or disable I2C slave control mode.
.It Fl -i2c-master Cm enable | disable
Enable or disable I2C master (USB-to-I2C gateway) mode.
.It Fl -i2c-set-address Ar ADDR
Set the I2C address the board answers to in slave mode.
.It Fl -i2c-write Ar ADDR Ar BYTE ...
Write between 1 and 60 bytes to the I2C slave at
.Ar ADDR .
.It Fl -i2c-read Ar ADDR Ar COUNT
Read up to 60 bytes from the I2C slave at
.Ar ADDR
and print one decimal number per line.
.El
.Ss Board commands and modifiers
.Bl -tag -width "--i2c-set-address ADDR"
.It Fl l
List the serial numbers of the attached YKUSH3 boards.
.It Fl s Ar SERIAL
Send the command to the board with serial number
.Ar SERIAL
instead of the first one the system enumerates.
.It Fl -no-wait
Fail at once with exit status 75 when the board is in use, instead of waiting
up to five seconds for it.
.It Fl -firmware-version
Print the firmware version of the board.
.It Fl -bootloader-version
Print the bootloader version of the board.
.It Fl -reset
Restart the board.
.It Fl -boot
Restart into the USB bootloader.
.It Fl v , Fl -version
Print the version of
.Nm .
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print the usage and option summary.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
The exit status follows
.Xr sysexits 3 :
.Bl -tag -width "101" -compact
.It Cm 0
Success; also
.Fl l
when no board is attached.
.It Cm 64
Invalid command line.
.It Cm 69
No board found, unknown serial number, board disconnected, HID driver
detached, or the board rejected the command.
.It Cm 74
No answer within the five second timeout, a truncated report, a transport
error, or writing to standard output failed.
.It Cm 75
The board is in use by another process (after waiting five seconds, or at once
with
.Fl -no-wait ) .
.It Cm 76
An answer from the board did not fit the request.
.It Cm 77
Permission denied opening the device node.
.It Cm 101
Internal panic.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Power port 2 down, read the state of all three downstream ports, and configure
port 2 to come up on the next reset:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
ykushctrl -s Y3N13808 -d 2
ykushctrl -g a
ykushctrl -c 2 1
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr flock 2 ,
.Xr sysexits 3
